We need an operator "->" which in reality is "invoke method",
but in the degenerate case (with no arguments) becomes "get value".

It is my opinion that, for any given object, between updates, the
value should be idempotent.  This means that if you want an incrementing
counter or anything like that, you need an explicit verb for that.

This is the simplest case I can think of.  A "blob" is a verb
provided by testmod that generates an object.  We can use its "name"
method to get back the name we provided.

	target showBlob
		blob "hello" => a_blob
		show (a_blob->name)

